# Achievement registry instructions

## Record format

The Data section is the source of truth. Each achievement is one three-line record followed by a blank line:

1. Steam API ID
2. Display name
3. Unlock description

Do not add headings, comments, or other lines inside the Data section.

## Writing standards

- Use a concise verb-object PascalCase Steam API ID.
- Prefer a short English historical allusion for the display name. Use Latin only when the expression is widely known.
- Write the description as an imperative sentence that states the exact unlock condition and ends with a period.
- For an event-based achievement, use `Complete the "EVENT NAME" mission.` as the description, substituting the
  exact English display name of the event.
- Use the collective perspective for possessives: write "our province," not "your province."

## Code implementation

- Unlock the achievement at the gameplay event or action that completes its stated condition.
- For an achievement unlocked by a gameplay event (`IGameEventConfig`), add `achievement: "ID"` to that event.
  The shared event handler unlocks it when the event is added for the player. Use the event's exact English display
  name in the Data description, and do not also call `unlockAchievement` for the same event.
- For achievements that are not represented by a game event, pass the exact Steam API ID from the Data section to
  `unlockAchievement("ID")` at the completion point.
- Direct `unlockAchievement` calls must be guarded so shared and headless code paths cannot unlock achievements for
  AI provinces. Event-based achievements already apply only to the player.
- Do not unlock an achievement when the player merely opens a screen, starts an action, or fails its condition.

## Icon generation

Choose an appropriate existing painting from `packages/client/src/assets/images/events/`. Consult
`packages/client/src/game/events/EventImages.ts` for the painting's subject and historical context.

Generate the achieved and unachieved icons with:

`npm run achievement -- "packages/client/src/assets/images/events/PAINTING.webp" ID`

The command must produce both required files:

- Achieved icon: `arts/achievements/ID.jpg`
- Unachieved icon: `arts/achievements/ID_.jpg`

## Steamworks synchronization

Restitutor's Steam App ID is `4431750`. Open its Achievement Configuration page in a signed-in in-app browser:

`https://partner.steamgames.com/apps/achievements/4431750`

Compare the Steamworks table with the Data section before making changes:

- Add only achievements whose Steam API IDs are missing.
- Do not alter an existing record when it already matches.
- If an existing record has a mismatched name, description, setting, or icon, report the difference and request
  direction before overwriting it.

For each missing achievement:

1. Select New Achievement.
2. Copy the Steam API ID, display name, and description exactly from the Data section.
3. Set Progress Stat to None and Set By to Client. Leave Hidden unchecked.
4. Save the new achievement before uploading icons. Steamworks rejects icon uploads for unsaved achievements.
5. Edit the saved achievement.
6. Upload `arts/achievements/ID.jpg` as the Achieved Icon.
7. Upload `arts/achievements/ID_.jpg` as the Unachieved Icon.
8. Save the achievement again after both uploads.

Leave all Steamworks changes unpublished for review unless the user explicitly requests publication.

## Verification checklist

Before finishing, verify that:

- Every Data record has either an exact `achievement: "ID"` on the correct game event or an exact
  `unlockAchievement("ID")` call at the correct action completion point.
- Every event-based achievement's Data description references the event's exact English display name.
- Every direct `unlockAchievement("ID")` call is guarded so only the player can unlock it.
- Every Data record has both required local icon files.
- Every Data record appears exactly once in the Steamworks table.
- Every Steamworks record has the exact API Name, display name, and description from this file.
- Every Steamworks record is set by Client, is not hidden, and has two hosted icons.
- No achievement edit form remains open or unsaved.

The Steamworks "Number of achievements" label may not include unpublished additions. Audit the visible table records
instead of relying on that label alone.

